As I was doing some background research for this article, I noted a
hallucination in one of Perplexity=E2=80=99s pages. The post reads: =E2=80=
=9C*Chinese-built
large language models now account for 61% of total token consumption on
OpenRouter.*=E2=80=9D In truth, the actual indicator is that Chinese models=
 make up
61% of the combined token consumption of the top ten models on OpenRouter.
I=E2=80=99m not trying to nit-pick here; this is the type of slop that will=
 become
more and more common, and it will be more and more important for people to
note the difference between =E2=80=9Cseemingly rigorous=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=
=9Cactually rigorous=E2=80=9D
content.
